      "venue": "Hacker News comment, September 2026, on a thread about an age-verification provider's SOC 2 claim. Text retrieved with HTML entities intact.",
      "speaker": "practitioner",
      "published": "2026-09-11",
      "pulled": "2026-09-17",
      "verbatim": "&gt; Yoti is an independently audited age verification provider for SOC2 compliance.<p>I worked for a consulting firm and I needed a client to get SOC2 compliant.<p>The way we did it was scarily easy. It was like a self questionnaire that was like &quot;we dont log PII&quot; and other stuff like that. I could have lied and said yes to everything and still got compliant. I thought I was gonna have a meeting with someone to audit my answers and codebase but instead I got a shiny badge after about an hour of answering questions.<p>Anyway, there are many SOC2 compliant companies that get pwnd so this isnt really reassuring in itself."
