      "url": "https://news.ycombinator.com/item?id=10199589",
      "title": "kgosser on the cost of proving HIPAA compliance",
      "venue": "Hacker News comment on the Heroku Private Spaces thread, 2015.",
      "speaker": "practitioner",
      "published": "2015-09-10",
      "pulled": "2026-09-17",
      "verbatim": "Speaking from a HIPAA point of view, the amount of complexity you must manage to build your own compliant environment on AWS is extremely high. HIPAA's controls account for block level encryption, managing your logs a certain way, and many many more things.<p>Furthermore, compliance is more than just doing the right thing. It's proving that you are compliant. There is immeasurable value with selecting a vendor who is audited to be HIPAA Compliant or HITRUST Certified because then the risk is offloaded to someone with credibility in the marketplace via a Business Associate Agreement.",
      "unused": "'compliance is more than just doing the right thing. It's proving that you are compliant' is the cleanest articulation of the category's premise found in the sweep, but at eleven years old it is too stale to carry a pain row. Kept as the vocabulary source behind the transparency framing in pain:the-answer-spreadsheet and as a lead for the regulated-segment re-run."
